title start
name: title-ecosystem-tui-configuration
kind: plan
tags: ecosystem tui configuration plan
Ecosystem TUI configuration plan
title end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-goal
Goal. One TUI configurator for the whole ecosystem, in the same
interface for every part. People never edit configuration files
by hand, which skips a whole class of problems. Colors come only
from the theme engine.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-state
State. Only the website part exists: settings-tui.rkt in this
folder edits notation/layouts/layout-settings.aiu and reloads the
page. Nothing else is configured yet, on purpose. The interface
is built once here so other parts do not need a new one.
paragraph end


paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-decided-floating
Decided. Each configurator is a floating full screen pane in the
multiplexer. It is never opened and never closed. It is only shown
and hidden by a key, so nothing loads when the key is pressed.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-decided-server
Decided. The server loads the settings data once and keeps it. It
changes only when a setting changes, otherwise it does no work.
The pane already has the data and is real time, so it appears
instantly. This is light for the server.
paragraph end


paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-decided-order
Decided. First make the website configurator a first class part:
the key, the floating pane and the server data. Only then move
forward. No other part is configured before that.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-decided-same-pattern
Decided. The same pattern, server loaded, floating full screen
pane, key to show and hide, is wanted for the AIU jump, which is
the custom zoxide inside the shell, and for the theme settings.
The pane is built once and reused for all of them.
paragraph end


paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-decided-key
Decided. Key e in the multiplexer Visual mode shows and hides the
settings float, beside 1 2 3 for the editor floats. Hiding never
closes it.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-state-pane
State. The settings pane is the fifth float of the multiplexer,
named settings, full size. It runs settings-pane.sh in this
folder, which starts the TUI once. Written, not yet confirmed on
screen. The TUI no longer runs stty size on every redraw.
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tui-open
Open, in this order. 1. Confirm key 4 on screen. 2. Server holds
the settings data and pushes changes, so the pane never loads. 3.
AIU jump on the same pattern. 4. Theme settings on the same
pattern. 5. The full feature plan for the other parts.
paragraph end
